---
import TopicPage from '../../../../components/TopicPage.astro';
import Widget from '../../../../components/Widget.astro';

const genCfg = {
  steps: [
    { math: '1 · Two families of generative models', note: 'GANs (2014): a forger and a detective train against each other until forgeries are indistinguishable. Diffusion (2020→): learn to remove noise step by step, then generate by running it backwards. Diffusion won the image race.' },
    { math: '2 · Latent space: the map of meanings', note: 'Generative models compress data into a latent space where nearby points are similar concepts. Interpolating between two latents morphs one face into another — the space itself is a learned geometry of concepts.' },
    { math: '3 · Text-to-image: language steering', note: 'CLIP (2021) learned to match images and text in one space; diffusion conditioned on those embeddings turns sentences into pictures (DALL·E, Stable Diffusion, Midjourney). The prompt is now a programming language for images.' },
    { math: '4 · Copyright and provenance are open problems', note: 'Models trained on artists\' work without consent; outputs resembling training data; watermarks (C2PA provenance) as countermeasures. Courts and markets are still deciding — a live legal frontier, not settled law.' },
  ],
};
---
<TopicPage slug="subjects/artificial-intelligence/expert/generative-models">
  <h2>The idea</h2>
  <p>
    Generative models <strong>learn a data distribution well enough to sample new examples from
    it</strong> — faces, art, music, code, molecules. They are the AI family behind image
    generation, music synthesis, drug design and every text generator. Understanding them means
    understanding both their creative power and their unresolved relationship to the data (and
    people) they learned from.
  </p>

  <Widget no="1" caption="the generative landscape: families, latent spaces, steering, open questions" widget="equationStep" config={genCfg} />

  <h2>The applications reshaping industries</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Drug and material discovery:</strong> generative models propose candidate molecules with desired properties, screened computationally before synthesis — compressing discovery pipelines from years toward months.</li>
    <li><strong>Creative workflows:</strong> image/video generation as iteration tools — concept art, storyboarding, prototyping. The displacement debate is real; the augmentation evidence is also real (both can be true, for different tasks).</li>
    <li><strong>Deepfakes are the shadow:</strong> voice cloning and face swaps enable fraud and disinformation — detection lags generation, so provenance standards (signed content credentials) are the durable defence being built.</li>
    <li><strong>Scientific generation is the quiet revolution:</strong> generating protein structures (AlphaFold's successor models), weather fields, and materials — generation as scientific hypothesis machine.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="sources"><strong>Sources:</strong> Goodfellow et al., NeurIPS (2014) GANs; Ho et al., NeurIPS (2020) diffusion; Ramesh et al. (DALL·E); Radford et al., CLIP (2021).</p>
</TopicPage>
